# Read Email — auto pipeline (operator minimal input)

**Chat scope:** Email processing chat only (`EMAIL-PROCESSING-AGENT.md`).

**Operator types only:** **login**, **RE** (first case of session), **PR** (each case end). See `.cursor/rules/operator-minimal-input.mdc`.

**Case 2+:** no typed RE — closeout listen + notify/stop hook auto-triggers 7-step + Auto-LF after operator clicks Sprinklr close-out.

**Always stick to the processing form:** Full 7-step output from **sprinklr-read-answer-email** SKILL.md.

### Auto-trigger (normal workday — no RE command)

| Trigger | Agent action (EMAIL) |
|---------|----------------------|
| **EMAIL sidetray click** (`CASE_ITEM_AUTO_CLICKED` → `SIDETRAY_EMAIL_PROCESSING_IMMEDIATE`) | Script **immediately** opens case + extract — **zero operator input** |
| **`--await-arm` extract** completes (`DETACHED_ARM_EXTRACT_READY` / `CUSTOMER EMAIL` + `RE_TEXT_ONLY_GATE`) | Agent **same workflow** immediately continues three-turn RE → Auto-LF → wait **PR** or transfer arm — **no new user message, no typed RE** |
| **First case after login** — operator types **RE** once | `run.py --once` → 7-step → Auto-LF → wait **PR** |
| **CALL** (`CHANNEL: CALL` / `CALL_LF_GATE`) | Auto-LF voice + close-out arm — no 7-step, no PR unless asked |

**Typed RE** = **first case only** (+ agent-internal `--once` / `--pickup` on failure — never ask operator).

### HARD BAN — EVERY EMAIL CASE: paste extract + 7-step (no exceptions)

**Every** CHANNEL: EMAIL Fall # — first case, every later case, after every Anwenden/Weiter/Extern/Next extract, every recovery `--once`:

1. You **MUST** write the full **7-step RE** as **visible chat text** for **that** Fall # — plain markdown in this chat. **Every time. New case = new 7-step.** Prior Fall # output does not satisfy this. **Do NOT paste the customer email body / Subject / From into chat** — operator sees it directly in Sprinklr; it is noise here.  
2. **Forbidden shortcuts:** Auto-LF only; “transfer done” one-liner; **“extracted — 7-step next”** / **“writing RE…”** without pasting; paste-ready reply without sections 1–5/7; tool-only turn with no extract/7-step text; pointing at `latest_extract.md` instead of pasting; skipping paste because “operator can scroll up” or “same session”.  
3. **Forbidden hiding:** Do **not** put extract/7-step only inside tool results, background-task panels, collapsed **“finished N background tasks”** / task dropdowns, or anything the user must click to expand. Extract + 7-step must appear as **normal chat prose** above the fold **for each case**.  
4. **Turn order (EMAIL) — repeat per Fall #:**  
 - **A:** Extract (`run.py` / await-arm) — tools only; **no** operator-facing one-liner.  
 - **B (immediate, no wait for operator):** paste **extract** + sections **1–7** as plain chat — **ZERO tools**. See `.cursor/rules/re-no-background-tasks-ui.mdc`.  
 - **C:** only after B is visible: `--play-ready`, **Auto-LF**, transfer arm **or** wait for **PR**.  
 - Operator recovery: **`RE SHOW`** / **`visible RE`** → re-print **extract + full 7-step** for the **current** Fall #; **`RE FILE`** → `show_latest_re.py`.  
5. Transfer-eligible EMAIL still gets extract + all 7 sections visible in chat (section 6 may be short forward notice).  
6. **CALL** does **not** use the email 7-step form (Auto-LF voice on CHANNEL detect).  

If you already ran Auto-LF / tools without a visible extract + 7-step for **this** Fall # in chat: **STOP**, paste extract + full 7-step now, then continue.

**AI model:** Prefer **Claude 4.6 Sonnet** for EMAIL RE. **Grok banned.** See `.cursor/rules/ai-model-stay-auto.mdc`.

## Detached arm (mandatory — why watches used to “die”)

Cursor **aborts** long-running agent shells (~20s) when a turn ends. That used to kill the in-shell Anwenden/Weiter/Extern watch → `ERROR: ANWENDEN WATCH DIED BEFORE EXTRACT` → `--once` recovery.

**Fix:** `--arm` / `--arm-weiter` / `--arm-extern` spawn a **detached** Windows process by default (`ARM_WATCH_DETACHED`). Cursor aborting the shell does **not** kill the listener. Log: `.cursor/state/arm_watch.log`.

| Step | Command | Expect |
|------|---------|--------|
| 1 | **Background** `run.py --closeout-anwenden` (post-PR) / `--closeout-weiter` / `--closeout-extern` / `--closeout-next` | `CLOSEOUT_LISTEN_ACTIVE` + `ARM_WATCH_DETACHED` + Dexter; notify on extract gate |
| 2 | Finishing quote only | `PR done` / `LF TR done` / `LF done` — operator clicks Sprinklr button only |
| 3 | Notify or stop-hook `[AUTO_PIPELINE]` | `DETACHED_ARM_EXTRACT_READY` + gate → **immediate** 7-step + Auto-LF (zero operator typing) |
| 3b | **EMAIL sidetray path** | On `CASE_ITEM_AUTO_CLICKED` → extract in same chain — immediate 7-step + Auto-LF |
| 4 | Full **7-step RE** + `--play-ready` + **Auto-LF** | On extract stdout / notify — never wait for operator RE/NEXT/LF |

- **Click-ready = Dexter + READY_FOR_YOUR_CLICK** — do not wait for await to finish before clicking.
- If **`--await-arm`** is aborted by Cursor → **re-run `--await-arm`** (detached watch still running).
- If log shows **`ERROR: NEXT CASE NOT OPEN`** → **`run.py --once`** on the visible case (arm already stopped).
- Use **`--once`** also if `ARM_WATCH_LOG` has **no** CUSTOMER EMAIL after timeout.
- **Never** start a second `--arm*` while a detached watch is still waiting.
- **`--foreground`** = legacy blocking watch (debug only).

### Next-case click (after Anwenden / Weiter / Weiterleiten)

Script remembers **closed Fall #**, skips that sidebar item, polls ~25s for a different case, retries if still console/same Fall. Hard fail → stop arm + `--once` tip (no second Weiterleiten wait).

## Normal workday

1. **login** → Case Tracker tab.
2. Operator **RE** once (first case) → 7-step (visible chat) + Auto-LF → **immediately** `--closeout-anwenden` (background + notify) → rest, awaiting PR or arm.
3. Operator **PR** → agent pastes reply only (arm already running). Quote: `PR done for #FALL_ID`.
4. Operator clicks **Anwenden** → arm fires → sidetray poll → new case → agent **auto** processes (CALL or EMAIL) — no operator input.
5. Repeat: operator types **PR** only. Agent handles everything else.

**Operator types:** **login**, **RE** (first case only), **PR**, **DONE**. Never **NEXT**, **LF**, or case 2+ **RE**.

## Full case lifecycle

```
[Monitoring active: arm fired → sidetray click]

EMAIL case:
  sidetray click → extract → 7-step visible in chat → Auto-LF
  → --closeout-anwenden (background, arm armed) → rest
  → await:  PR (paste) | reiteration (change reply/LF) | arm fires (no reply needed)
  → arm fires → [Monitoring active] → next case

CALL case:
  case pops up → CHANNEL: CALL → Auto-LF voice
  → --closeout-next/weiter (arm armed) → rest
  → await:  BRIEF (optional KB/TM lookup from operator) | arm fires
  → arm fires → [Monitoring active] → next case

Transfer (EMAIL or CALL):
  Auto-LF TR → --closeout-weiter/extern (arm armed) → rest
  → arm fires → [Monitoring active] → next case
```

**PR is independent of arming.** Arm is already running when PR arrives. Agent pastes and finishes — arm detects Anwenden when operator clicks it.

### HARD — Prowler without RE/LF

**Prowler = extract DONE.** Agent **must** continue via shell notify or stop-hook `[AUTO_PIPELINE]` — agent runs `--pickup` internally if needed. **Never** ask operator to type anything.

## Recovery — when user sends **RE** / **re** / **RE SHOW** / **RE FILE**

**Hard rule:** Typed **RE** = **manual re-extract** (`--once`) or visibility recovery — **not** the default path. It must **never** arm Anwenden.

1. Run default RE entrypoint:
   ```powershell
   Set-Location "c:\Users\PC ENTER\Desktop\Citrix"; uv run python .cursor/skills/sprinklr-read-answer-email/run.py
   ```
   Expect **`MODE: --once`** and either `FIRST_RE_ONCE_CONSUMED` (after login) or `RE_ONCE_DEFAULT`. **Trust script stdout:** `CHANNEL: CALL` + `CALL_LF_GATE` → voice Auto-LF + Next (no 7-step). `CHANNEL: EMAIL` + `CUSTOMER EMAIL` + `RE_TEXT_ONLY_GATE` → three-turn 7-step RE (see `sprinklr-call-vs-email.mdc`).
2. **Do not** run `--arm` / `--await-arm` on typed RE. Arms run after Auto-LF / PR close-out (below).
3. **Audio:**
   - **Armed auto-RE start:** After Anwenden / Weiter / Extern / Next → sidetray poll (`SIDETRAY_WATCH_ARMED`) → **EMAIL:** click sidetray item; **CALL:** skip click, wait for overlay (`SIDETRAY_CALL_AUTO_OPEN`) → extract begins → Prowler (`ARMED_RE_START_SOUND`).
   - **RE ready (after section 7):** Hook plays book-opening cue (`RE_READY_SOUND`) when `RE_PENDING_SOUND` was set — case is ready to read.
   - **PR done / LF TR done:** Finishing quotes → Dexter (`PR_LF_DONE_SOUND`).
   - Manual: **`sound`** → `--play-ready`.
4. After 7-step + `--play-ready`: **Auto-LF** (do not wait for typed `LF`). See `.cursor/rules/lf-log-form.mdc`.
5. **EMAIL non-transfer:** wait for user **PR** → after paste succeeds → background **`--closeout-anwenden`** + notify. Quote `PR done for #FALL_ID`.
6. **EMAIL / CALL transfer:** after Auto-LF Transfer Ja → background **`--closeout-weiter`** / **`--closeout-extern`**. Quote `LF TR done for #FALL_ID`.
7. **CALL:** on CHANNEL detect → **immediately Auto-LF** voice → background **`--closeout-next`**. Quote `LF done for #FALL_ID`. Do **not** wait for BRIEF.

### Explicit modes

| Command | Behavior |
|---------|----------|
| `run.py` / typed **RE** | First case / recovery **`--once`** — never arm Anwenden |
| `run.py --once` | Same (explicit recovery) |
| `run.py --closeout-anwenden` | **Post-PR:** arm Anwenden + block until extract (background + notify) |
| `run.py --closeout-weiter` | Post-transfer queue: arm Weiter + block until extract |
| `run.py --closeout-extern` | Post-transfer email: arm Extern + block until extract |
| `run.py --closeout-next` | Post-CALL LF: arm Next + block until extract |
| `run.py --arm` / `--arm-*` | Legacy arm-only (prefer `--closeout-*`) |
| `run.py --await-arm` / `--pickup` | Agent-internal listen/recovery — **never** ask operator |
| `run.py --foreground` | Debug only: blocking in-shell watch |

## After extract: paste extract + 7-step + Auto-LF (mandatory)

Every EMAIL extract (auto after login, `--await-arm`, or recovery `--once`):

1. **Immediately** write the full **7-step RE** as visible chat text (turn-B — operator must see it without expanding any dropdown / background-task panel / file). **Never** stop after extract with only an ack. **Do NOT paste the customer email body / Subject / From into chat** — operator sees it in Sprinklr; it is noise here.  
2. **Only then** **`re_complete_sound.py --play-ready`**  
3. **Only then** **Auto-LF** for this Fall # (Transfer Nein or Ja per §3) — user does **not** type `LF`  
4. If Auto-LF prints **`PAUSE_AUTO_LF`** + **`LF_CONTINUE_AFTER_SPEICHERN_ARMED`** (exit `3`): warn user to click Speichern for the **previous** LF; Auto-LF for the **current** Fall # continues automatically — run **`fill_case_tracker.py --await-speichern-continue`**, then on **`CONTINUE_LF_DONE`** do transfer arm or wait for **PR**. Do **not** require a manual Auto-LF retry after Speichern.  
5. **Immediately after Auto-LF** (both transfer and non-transfer): start background close-out arm — do **not** wait for PR to arm.
   - Non-transfer: **`--closeout-anwenden`** (background + notify). Rest and await PR or reiteration.
   - Transfer: **`--closeout-weiter`** / **`--closeout-extern`** (no PR needed).

**Auto-LF / tool runs must never replace, precede, or hide the 7-step behind Cursor task UI.**

Every CALL on CHANNEL detect: Auto-LF `--channel voice` → arm Next (or Weiter/Extern if transfer). BRIEF is optional and never blocks Auto-LF.

## OPERATOR INPUTS ONLY (hard)

**Allowed chat commands:** **login**, **RE** (first case only), **PR**, **DONE**.

**FORBIDDEN:** Asking the operator for **NEXT**, **RE** (case 2+), **LF**, or any continue/pickup command. Agent recovers internally (`--pickup` / re-await). Operator only clicks Sprinklr UI (Senden / Anwenden / Weiter / Next / Speichern).

## After **PR** (EMAIL non-transfer)

Arm (`--closeout-anwenden`) already started at Auto-LF time. PR just pastes the reply:

1. Paste reply + verify clean.
2. Quote: `PR done for #FALL_ID`.
3. **No new arm command.** Arm is already running from Auto-LF step.
4. Operator clicks Senden (independent) + Anwenden (arm reacts) in any order.

**Senden is independent** — not an arm criterion, no ordering with Anwenden.

### Close-out arm table (all paths — arm starts at Auto-LF, not at PR)

| Case type | Close-out command (at Auto-LF time) | Operator Sprinklr click |
|---|---|---|
| **EMAIL non-transfer** | **`--closeout-anwenden`** (background + notify) | Anwenden |
| **EMAIL transfer (queue)** | **`--closeout-weiter`** | Transfer UI → exact Weiter |
| **EMAIL transfer (email `@`)** | **`--closeout-extern`** | Externer Transfer → Weiterleiten |
| **CALL non-transfer** | **`--closeout-next`** | exact Next |
| **CALL transfer** | **`--closeout-weiter`** / **`--closeout-extern`** | Weiter / Weiterleiten |

**Prowler = extract done** — never stop idle; agent fixes internally; never push recovery commands to the operator.

Do **not** arm twice for the same close-out. Do **not** start a new arm on PR — arm was already started at Auto-LF.

## 7-step output

**Language:** Sections **1–5** and **7** → **English** (to the operator). Section **6** → **German only** (customer). All other agent chat to the user → English. See `.cursor/rules/agent-english-user-customer-german.mdc`.

1. Customer summary (EN)  
2. Verification (EN) — **compressed** 2–4 lines; status + key ids only; no tables (`.cursor/rules/re-verification-format.mdc`)  
3. Transfer eligibility (EN)  
4a/4b. Backend / instructions (EN)  
5. Instructions on handling case (EN)  
6. Your response to customer (**German**, code block; **chat** soft-wrap ~72 for vertical read; **PR** uses mail-format length — not chat wraps)  
7. Summary of response (EN) — then run **`re_complete_sound.py --play-ready`** (book) — then **Auto-LF**

## Integrity

- One visible case only; discard prior Fall # context on each new **RE**.
- PR pastes latest RE for the **same visible Fall #** only.
- Watch loop must **not** steal browser focus (`bring_to_front`) while waiting.
- **No monitor fallback:** If Anwenden-gated RE fails, **stop and report**. Do **not** fall into continuous `monitor_emails` / `get_new_emails` loops.

## Rollback

If this experiment fails or you dislike it, in the **instructions** chat type **`revert last`** — restores checkpoint `.cursor/revert-checkpoints/pre-anwenden-re/`.

